      script: "At Alorica, I was sent to Davao to investigate low CSAT for a high-end US retail fashion store account. At first, it could have looked like an agent communication problem, so training would have been the easy assumption.\n\nI interviewed agents and supervisors and found that the real issue was more technical and process-related. When customers needed to replace an item, they had to return it, wait for the refund, and then repurchase the same item. That process was effortful for the customer and hard for agents to explain without sounding unhelpful.\n\nAs an instructional designer, I could not redesign the client's workflow. What I could do was create an empathetic script that helped agents guide customers through the process with more patience and clarity. But in the client meeting, I also named the underlying issue: the process itself was creating customer effort. The client acknowledged it and considered it.\n\nAfter I returned to Manila, CSAT improved, with feedback highlighting the agents' patience and professionalism. I take that as a good lesson. Training helped mitigate the issue, but it was not the whole answer. A course cannot fully fix a process that makes the right customer experience hard to deliver.",
